!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/a-kind-of-a-namespace-type-names-its-values-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.12"
  description: """
    A slot over `T` holds a name exactly when the type of the named entry's value IS-A `T`, and the spelling
    makes no difference. `api` is a namespace type and no constructor, so the values it admits are values:
    `kind<api>` is the same reference as `ref<api>`, and `myops`, whose value is of `api`, is a name it holds.
    """
  valid: {
    binds: [apis api_slot api_held]
  }
}
